 "_about": "PLAN.md §23 WP 13.4 — gate `page-equals-run`. A fixture project that exercises every source a master-backed /policies cell can show: a /policies override, the item master, a value derived from the lanes (cost, price, demand), the line-rate capacity derivation, the engine's declared default, a BOM-only material with no master row and a supplier with no master row, a Supplier-row lead time over its lane (S2::M1) and a lane with no lead time (S3::M3). `engine` is what scsim's mapper gives each entity field, with its source — GENERATED by sim-worker/tests/test_page_equals_run.py (REGEN=1) and checked by it on every run; src/lib/policies/__tests__/pageEqualsRun.test.ts resolves every grid cell through the page's own resolver and requires zero differences. `policy.defaults` is the page's DEFAULT_BUNDLE, as a policy version now stores it (§4 D204 a). Since PLAN.md §24 WP 14.2 it also exercises the Customer stage's demand cells: a row spec from the data (C1::P1 normal, C2::P2 triangular), an override (C1::P2), a forecast series, and rows the data leaves empty. Since PLAN.md §25 WP 15.3 it exercises a lane's lead-time shape: a triangular lane from the upload (S2::M2, whose Lead time is the bounds' mean), a Supplier-row override (S1::M1 normal with its CV), the material's lognormal under a lane that states none (S2::M1), and a lane that is deterministic by default (S3::M3).",
